# Route type declarations written by the Vite plugin on every configResolved,
# beside the pages directory (so `src/` for the default `src/app`). A plain
# `vite build` rewrites them; they are derived from the folder tree and must
# never be committed. The pattern is unanchored to cover every fixture, the
# example app, and any project scaffolded inside the repository - which is also
# why the plugin refuses to overwrite a `routes.d.ts` it did not generate, and
# why a hand-authored file of that name has to live somewhere else. The old
# generated name stays listed until the plugin has removed those copies.
routes.d.ts
virtual-next-vite-router.d.ts
# Artifacts of building the compatibility fixture locally
# Temporary project dirs created by the route-types test
test/route-types-*/
# Temporary project dirs created by the lazyLayouts end-to-end test
test/lazy-e2e-*/
# Playwright output of the browser suite (reports, traces, screenshots)
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
# Page folder the HMR test creates and removes while the dev server runs, so the
# route table really changes under the watcher. Written inside the fixture app and
# never part of it.
test/browser-app/src/app/hmr-live/
# Throwaway copy of the fixture app the HMR project serves on its own port, so a
# structural route change cannot reload the server the other browser tests use.
test/browser-app/hmr-run/
